{# The layout every page of the interaction plane extends (architecture §5.2): the document, its language
   (the locale of the interaction, architecture §5.7) and the blocks a page fills. The bundle ships the
   structure and the words, never a stylesheet or a script: an application gives the pages their look by
   overriding this one file under templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/layout.html.twig, and the pages of the
   bundle come with it; a page it wants otherwise is overridden the same way, by its name. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block title %}{% endblock %}</title>
    {% block head %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body>
    {% block body %}
        <main>
            <h1>{% block heading %}{{ block('title') }}{% endblock %}</h1>
            {% block content %}{% endblock %}
        </main>
    {% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
